    description: "WHAT (owner ruling on decision 9). PRs run every selected test; nothing is cut. The budget machinery is built as a REPORT only, so that its numbers exist if the owner later wants to switch a cut on:\n- a ranking of the selected tests, cheapest covering test first (the timing store exists);\n- the at-risk statements of a change: statements all of whose covering tests pass through the change;\n- the inferred whole-tree coverage (the last full run's coverage minus at-risk statements not re-run), printed beside the measured figure.\nENFORCEMENT IS OUT OF SCOPE: it is a later switch for the owner, and decisions 10 (the coverage claim) and 11 (the spot check) are not ruled.\n\nEVIDENCE AND ITS LIMIT. Change plus at-risk fit 150 test-seconds in 1,497 of 1,500 sampled ONE-FUNCTION changes. That does not transfer to PRs: 16 of 37 replayed PRs need 109 test-seconds or more on changed statements alone. And inferred coverage is not the same as tests passing: it says nothing about tests that run the changed statement and would be cut.\n\nCLOSE CONDITION. The report on a real PR, with the inferred and the measured figure; where they differ, why. A test with a mutation control for the at-risk computation.\n\nSOURCE. ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fast_smart_test_plan_11152026.md; the owner's rulings of 2026-11-17 are its second 'Made' table. Measurements: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fast_smart_test_followup_11172026/README.md, slice_graph_11152026/README.md, stale_graph_1a_11152026/README.md, fast_smart_test_11152026/README.md (the 37-PR replay)."  # 521d
